      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2011 Hanley & Belfus. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Cognitive-behavioral therapy (CBT) is a psychological treatment that emphasizes the interrelation among thoughts, behaviors, feelings, and sensations. CBT has been proved effective not only for treatment of psychological illness but also for teaching adaptive coping strategies in the context of chronic illnesses, including chronic pain. The present article provides general information on CBT, specific information on CBT for pain, as well as guidelines and strategies for using CBT for hand and arm pain patients, as part of multidisciplinary care models."
      },
